Rule 1: Secure Shell Access Protocol (TCP Port 22)

Ingress access is strictly confined and authorized exclusively for the designated

administrative client IP address (192.168.29.228/32). Accurate modification of

the source IP address is a critical requisite for successful operational deployment.

-A ufw-user-input -p tcp --dport 22 -s 192.168.29.228 -j ACCEPT

Rule 2: HyperText Transfer Protocol (HTTP) Access (TCP Port 80)

Standard web service traffic is permitted from any originating network source,

provided that an active web server application deployment is in operation.

-A ufw-user-input -p tcp --dport 80 -j ACCEPT

Rule 3: Loopback Interface Traffic Exemption

Internal host communication conducted over the local loopback interface (lo) is

unconditionally granted acceptance to ensure requisite inter-process functionality.

-A ufw-user-input -i lo -j ACCEPT